 300:Middlewares/ST/STM32_WPAN/ble/core/ble_legacy.h **** /**
 301:Middlewares/ST/STM32_WPAN/ble/core/ble_legacy.h ****  * @brief ACI_GATT_ALLOW_READ
 302:Middlewares/ST/STM32_WPAN/ble/core/ble_legacy.h ****  * Allow the GATT server to send a response to a read request from a client.
 303:Middlewares/ST/STM32_WPAN/ble/core/ble_legacy.h ****  * The application has to send this command when it receives the
 304:Middlewares/ST/STM32_WPAN/ble/core/ble_legacy.h ****  * ACI_GATT_READ_PERMIT_REQ_EVENT or ACI_GATT_READ_MULTI_PERMIT_REQ_EVENT. This
 305:Middlewares/ST/STM32_WPAN/ble/core/ble_legacy.h ****  * command indicates to the stack that the response can be sent to the client.
 306:Middlewares/ST/STM32_WPAN/ble/core/ble_legacy.h ****  * So if the application wishes to update any of the attributes before they are
 307:Middlewares/ST/STM32_WPAN/ble/core/ble_legacy.h ****  * read by the client, it must update the characteristic values using the
 308:Middlewares/ST/STM32_WPAN/ble/core/ble_legacy.h ****  * ACI_GATT_UPDATE_CHAR_VALUE and then give this command. The application
 309:Middlewares/ST/STM32_WPAN/ble/core/ble_legacy.h ****  * should perform the required operations within 30 seconds. Otherwise the GATT
 310:Middlewares/ST/STM32_WPAN/ble/core/ble_legacy.h ****  * procedure will be timeout.
 311:Middlewares/ST/STM32_WPAN/ble/core/ble_legacy.h ****  *
 312:Middlewares/ST/STM32_WPAN/ble/core/ble_legacy.h ****  * @param Connection_Handle Specifies the ATT bearer for which the command
 313:Middlewares/ST/STM32_WPAN/ble/core/ble_legacy.h ****  *        applies.
 314:Middlewares/ST/STM32_WPAN/ble/core/ble_legacy.h ****  *        Values:
ARM GAS  C:\Users\Nathan\AppData\Local\Temp\cc7slxkI.s 			page 7


 315:Middlewares/ST/STM32_WPAN/ble/core/ble_legacy.h ****  *        - 0x0000 ... 0x0EFF: Unenhanced ATT bearer (the parameter is the
 316:Middlewares/ST/STM32_WPAN/ble/core/ble_legacy.h ****  *          connection handle)
 317:Middlewares/ST/STM32_WPAN/ble/core/ble_legacy.h ****  *        - 0xEA00 ... 0xEA3F: Enhanced ATT bearer (the LSB-byte of the
 318:Middlewares/ST/STM32_WPAN/ble/core/ble_legacy.h ****  *          parameter is the connection-oriented channel index)
